        "tip": "Spans are how you build “one big card, several small ones” layouts without extra wrappers."
      },
      {
        "title": "Centering with grid",
        "body": "`place-items` positions every item inside its cell. `center` is the shortest way to center anything in CSS.",
        "demo": {
          "base": "display:grid;min-height:180px;",
          "kids": [
            {
              "s": "background:#4338CA;color:#FFFFFF;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;text-align:center;",
              "t": "Hi"
            }
          ],
          "show": {
            ".box": [
              "display: grid"
            ]
          },
          "knobs": [
            {
              "prop": "place-items",
              "opts": [
                "normal",
                "start",
                "center",
                "end"
              ],
              "target": "parent",
              "sel": ".box",
              "start": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "tip": "`place-items` is shorthand for `align-items` + `justify-items`. In grid both apply, so one line centers both ways."
